# llm — an impure-boundary PORT for language-model completion, declared once
# and used by any aggregate that asks a model to write something. Two-color
# rule : sync domain, async adapter, NEVER a lock — every async concern lives
# at the adapter edge, never in the synchronous core.
#
# Signal is EFFECT, WITH A VERDICT (unlike tts's fire-and-forget) : the
# aggregate EMITS an event carrying the prompt, the adapter completes the
# prompt OUT-OF-PROCESS, and the completion RE-ENTERS the domain as a verdict
# command (success "Agg.RecordCompletion"). This is the payment shape, not the
# tts shape : the family declares `produces :response_text`, and the bind
# carries a `do success/failure end` block whose success verdict receives the
# `response_text` the handler emits.
#
# The how-verb is `completed_by`, hung off the aggregate FQN with its
# triggering event (`on:`). The config FIELDS the adapters carry are NAMED
# here ; their per-deployment VALUES live in .world (backend test|claude|
# ollama, model, max_tokens, prompt_template). The family never names its
# adapters (the inverted arrow lives in .adapter).
#
# slice-1 NOTE : `signal :effect` is KEPT — signal retirement is a later slice.
Hecks.family "llm" do
  verb   "completed_by"
  signal :effect
  field  :backend
  field  :model
  field  :max_tokens
  field  :prompt_template
  produces :response_text
end
